# text = Therefore, if it were possible that you could have just men to be your kings, who would establish the laws of God, and judge this people according to his commandments, yea, if ye could have men for your kings who would do even as my father Benjamin did for this people-- I say unto you, if this could always be the case then it would be expedient that ye should always have kings to rule over you.
# sent_id = 906
# llm_note = Highly complex conditional. Main root = "say" (token 59). First conditional "if it were possible..." is advcl of "say". Second conditional "if this could always be the case" is also advcl of main consequent "would be" (token 73). "I say unto you" is a parenthetical. "it were possible that..." — expletive "it", "possible" adj, "that you could have" = csubj. "who would establish...and judge" = acl:relcl on "kings" (token 16). "yea, if ye could have men" = second conditional parallel. "Benjamin" = appos of "father". "--" is punctuation attached to prior clause. "it would be expedient that" = expletive construction.
