# text = And he enacteth laws, and sendeth them forth among his people, yea, laws after the manner of his own wickedness; and whosoever doth not obey his laws he causeth to be destroyed; and whosoever doth rebel against him he will send his armies against them to war, and if he can he will destroy them; and thus an unrighteous king doth pervert the ways of all righteousness.
# sent_id = 917
# llm_note = Long paratactic sentence with many conj clauses. Root = "enacteth" (token 3). "sendeth" = conj of "enacteth". "yea, laws after the manner" = appos of "laws" (token 4). "whosoever doth not obey...he causeth" — fronted free relative (whosoever clause) as dislocated, "he" is main nsubj of "causeth". Similarly "whosoever doth rebel...he will send". "causeth to be destroyed" = causative xcomp. "to war" = purpose/obl. "thus an unrighteous king doth pervert" = final conj clause.
