# text = Now it is not common that the voice of the people desireth anything contrary to that which is right; but it is common for the lesser part of the people to desire that which is not right; therefore this shall ye observe and make it your law-- to do your business by the voice of the people.
# sent_id = 920
# llm_note = Two parallel expletive "it is (not) common that/for" constructions. "desireth" = archaic 3sg. "contrary to that which is right" — "contrary" is adj nmod of "anything"; "to that which is right" is obl of "contrary". Second clause: "it is common for the lesser part...to desire" — "for...to" infinitive as csubj. "therefore this shall ye observe and make it your law--" — "this" is obj of "observe" (fronted); "observe and make" are conj verbs. "to do your business by the voice of the people" = appositive or elaboration of "law" (acl).
